    {
      "kind": "skill",
      "sigil": true,
      "form": "section",
      "line": 104,
      "attrs": {
        "when": "turning findings into an answer",
        "name": "synthesis"
      },
      "body": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "text": "\nLead with the answer in one sentence. Then the evidence, one claim per\nparagraph, each with its citation at the end. Then what you are unsure of\nand why. Then what you did not read.\n\n### Disagreement\n\nWhen two sources disagree, show both, say which is primary, and say which\nyou would act on and why. NEVER: pick one silently.\n\n### Confidence\n\nUse exactly three words for confidence: *established* (two primary\nsources), *reported* (one source, or only untrusted ones), *unclear*\n(sources disagree or are silent). Put the word in the first sentence.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "skill",
      "sigil": true,
      "form": "section",
      "line": 121,
      "attrs": {
        "when": "writing any citation",
        "name": "citation-format"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "sigil": false,
          "form": "container",
          "line": 127,
          "attrs": {
            "title": "A well-cited paragraph"
          },
          "body": {
            "type": "markdown",
            "text": "The export job retries three times with exponential backoff before failing\n(Handbook › Exports › Retry policy). A resolved ticket describes a case where\nthe third retry succeeded after a nine-minute wait (T-3310), which is\nconsistent with the documented cap of ten minutes. *Established.*"
          }
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "text": "\nName the source, then the section or heading, in parentheses at the end of\nthe sentence. For a ticket, the ticket id. For a web page, the page title\nand the date you read it.\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "glossary",
      "sigil": false,
      "form": "container",
      "line": 136,
      "attrs": {},
      "body": {
        "type": "deflist",
        "entries": [
          {
            "term": "Primary source",
            "definition": "Written by the owning team and reviewed. The handbook and the runbooks."
          },
          {
            "term": "Claim",
            "definition": "One sentence that could be true or false. Every claim gets a citation."
          },
          {
            "term": "Corroboration",
            "definition": "A second source, independent of the first, that says the same thing."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
